Package: netkit
Type: Package
Title: Network Analysis and Visualization Toolkit
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R:
    person("Alex", "Gallinat", email = "alex.gaoc@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A collection of tools for analyzing and visualizing networks.
    Summarizes global topology, identifies hubs, bottlenecks and community
    structure, and classifies nodes into connectivity roles following
    Guimera and Amaral (2005) <doi:10.1038/nature03288>. Propagates influence
    from seed nodes using Laplacian smoothing, heat-kernel and
    random-walk-with-restart diffusion, with permutation-based empirical
    p-values, and simulates network robustness under progressive node removal.
    Matrix operations use sparse representations throughout so that the methods
    remain usable on large graphs.
